  "character_bible": "The recurring fictional chalk-line figure is an anonymous adult Japanese person shown with an unchanged round featureless head, slim neutral body proportions, simple off-white chalk-like outline, black charcoal clothing blocks, and restrained dot eyes only when emotional orientation requires them. Keep the figure gender-ambiguous, age-neutral adult, non-glamorous, and free of identifiable real-person traits. The figure's posture carries the psychology: forward-leaning shoulders and extended arms when over-helping, rigid chest and closed elbows when suppressing vulnerability, lowered head and compressed torso when guilt appears, and gradually more balanced standing posture during individuation. The dominant prop is one large black umbrella with a simple recognizable silhouette; it may shelter another small anonymous silhouette, tilt away from the helper, become heavy, or cast a shadow, but it must remain visually consistent. The helper can be shown both outside the umbrella in rain and inside a shared shelter, but never becomes a superhero or rescuer caricature. Supporting people are small, anonymous black silhouettes with no faces or distinguishing details. Gold appears only as a tiny controlled accent near the sheltered person, the umbrella interior, or the figure's chest when the hidden need becomes symbolically visible. No character speaks through visible text.",
  "environment_bible": "All environments exist inside the same charcoal-black and warm off-white paper universe. Prefer sparse symbolic spaces over literal rooms: rain-filled open fields, shallow pools of ink, a quiet threshold, a circular pool of light, a long empty path, or an abstract interior suggested by one floor line and one shadow. Backgrounds should use broad off-white paper fields integrated with charcoal ink fades rather than separate panels or cinematic location changes. Rain is thin, directional charcoal strokes, never a realistic storm; shadows are oversized, soft-edged, and psychologically expressive, sometimes detached from the figure or reaching back toward the chest. Maintain generous negative space around the central gesture so the emotional contradiction remains legible. If a practical object is necessary, reduce it to a single symbolic outline and keep it text-free. Avoid offices, hospitals, classrooms, bedrooms, busy streets, phones, laptops, notebooks, calendars, signs, readable documents, and explanatory infographics. Lighting is mostly diffuse paper brightness against charcoal masses, with one small warm gold accent used sparingly. Environmental continuity should make the umbrella, rain, shadow, paper grain, and gold point feel like recurring visual evidence of one inner process, while remaining explicitly symbolic.",
  "opening_visual_contract": {
